@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-registrar`

-- g4-tests-registrar.l4: tests for g4-registrar.l4 (s.19).  Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of s.19
-- (inputs/law.wiki lines 160-163) before the module was run; see work/g4/expectations.md and FRAGMENT-G4.md.
-- Each #ASSERT is one scenario.  A DEONTIC has no equality, so each #TRACE carries its expected outcome in the
-- `-- EXPECT` comment above it, which work/g4/trace-expect.py compares with what `l4 run --json` reports.

§ `Tests for section 19`

§§ `Section 19(a): the appointment`

-- Fields, in the order of the DECLARE: the Minister appointed the person | an employee of the Ministry | notice was published.
`a Ministry employee appointed by the Minister, notice published` MEANS `Appointment of a Registrar` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a Ministry employee appointed by the Minister, no notice yet`    MEANS `Appointment of a Registrar` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`an outsider appointed by the Minister`                           MEANS `Appointment of a Registrar` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`a Ministry employee named by someone other than the Minister`    MEANS `Appointment of a Registrar` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 19(a) — the person was appointed to hold the Registrar's powers` `a Ministry employee appointed by the Minister, notice published`
-- Reading taken (F-19a): publication is not a condition of the appointment.
#ASSERT `s 19(a) — the person was appointed to hold the Registrar's powers` `a Ministry employee appointed by the Minister, no notice yet`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(a) — the person was appointed to hold the Registrar's powers` `an outsider appointed by the Minister`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(a) — the person was appointed to hold the Registrar's powers` `a Ministry employee named by someone other than the Minister`

-- The alternative reading: the appointment counts only once notice was published.
#ASSERT `s 19(a), alternative reading — the appointment counts only once notice of it was published` `a Ministry employee appointed by the Minister, notice published`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(a), alternative reading — the appointment counts only once notice of it was published` `a Ministry employee appointed by the Minister, no notice yet`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(a), alternative reading — the appointment counts only once notice of it was published` `an outsider appointed by the Minister`

-- The Minister appoints an employee at day 3: the duty to publish stands.
-- EXPECT STANDING publish notice of the appointment of the Registrar in Reshumot
#TRACE `s 19(a) — the Minister must appoint, from among the Ministry's employees, a person to hold the Registrar's powers` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a person to hold the Registrar's powers` `the Minister` "Dana" TRUE AT 3

-- The Minister appoints, then publishes: fulfilled.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(a) — the Minister must appoint, from among the Ministry's employees, a person to hold the Registrar's powers` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a person to hold the Registrar's powers` `the Minister` "Dana" TRUE AT 3
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `publish notice of the appointment of the Registrar in Reshumot` `the Minister` "Dana" AT 9

-- Notice about a different person does not discharge the duty.
-- EXPECT STANDING publish notice of the appointment of the Registrar in Reshumot
#TRACE `s 19(a) — the Minister must appoint, from among the Ministry's employees, a person to hold the Registrar's powers` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a person to hold the Registrar's powers` `the Minister` "Dana" TRUE AT 3
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `publish notice of the appointment of the Registrar in Reshumot` `the Minister` "Eli" AT 9

-- Appointing a person who is not an employee is not performance: the duty to appoint still stands.
-- EXPECT STANDING appoint a person to hold the Registrar's powers
#TRACE `s 19(a) — the Minister must appoint, from among the Ministry's employees, a person to hold the Registrar's powers` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a person to hold the Registrar's powers` `the Minister` "Dana" FALSE AT 3

-- No time is stated, so waiting breaches nothing: the duty stands (s.19(a) has no WITHIN, and none is invented).
-- EXPECT STANDING appoint a person to hold the Registrar's powers
#TRACE `s 19(a) — the Minister must appoint, from among the Ministry's employees, a person to hold the Registrar's powers` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 3650)

-- The alternative actor for the notice: the Ministry publishes.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(a), alternative reading — the Ministry must publish notice of the appointment of the Registrar in Reshumot` "Dana" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Ministry` DOES `publish notice of the appointment of the Registrar in Reshumot` `the Ministry` "Dana" AT 5

§§ `Section 19(b): the Registrar's consent to a study programme`

-- Fields: the programme | a final certificate of the s.6(a)(4) kind can be obtained | the Registrar consented.
`a diploma programme the Registrar consented to`   MEANS `Study programme under section 19(b)` OF "diploma", TRUE, TRUE
`a diploma programme the Registrar did not consent to` MEANS `Study programme under section 19(b)` OF "diploma", TRUE, FALSE
`a short course that leads to no final certificate, no consent` MEANS `Study programme under section 19(b)` OF "short course", FALSE, FALSE
`a short course that leads to no final certificate, consent given` MEANS `Study programme under section 19(b)` OF "short course", FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 19(b) — the study programme needs the Registrar's consent` `a diploma programme the Registrar consented to`
#ASSERT `s 19(b) — the study programme needs the Registrar's consent` `a diploma programme the Registrar did not consent to`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(b) — the study programme needs the Registrar's consent` `a short course that leads to no final certificate, no consent`

#ASSERT `s 19(b) — the study programme has the Registrar's consent` `a diploma programme the Registrar consented to`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(b) — the study programme has the Registrar's consent` `a diploma programme the Registrar did not consent to`

#ASSERT `s 19(b) — the study programme satisfies the requirement of the Registrar's consent` `a diploma programme the Registrar consented to`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(b) — the study programme satisfies the requirement of the Registrar's consent` `a diploma programme the Registrar did not consent to`
-- A programme that does not need the consent satisfies the requirement with or without it.
#ASSERT `s 19(b) — the study programme satisfies the requirement of the Registrar's consent` `a short course that leads to no final certificate, no consent`
#ASSERT `s 19(b) — the study programme satisfies the requirement of the Registrar's consent` `a short course that leads to no final certificate, consent given`

-- The power to consent exists for a programme that needs it, and the Registrar's permission left unused breaches nothing.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(b) — the Registrar may give consent to the study programme` `a diploma programme the Registrar did not consent to` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `give the Registrar's consent to a study programme` `the Registrar` "diploma" AT 4

-- EXPECT STANDING give the Registrar's consent to a study programme
#TRACE `s 19(b) — the Registrar may give consent to the study programme` `a diploma programme the Registrar did not consent to` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- A programme that needs no consent gives the Registrar no power to consent: nothing is standing.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(b) — the Registrar may give consent to the study programme` `a short course that leads to no final certificate, no consent` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `Section 19(c)(1): recognition of a foreign qualification`

-- Fields: description | from a foreign institution | in the Registrar's opinion scope and content match
--         | the Registrar recognised it | the recognition was made conditional | the condition was met.
`a foreign degree whose scope and content match`      MEANS `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` OF "degree", TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a foreign degree whose scope and content do not match` MEANS `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` OF "degree", TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a qualification from an Israeli institution`          MEANS `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` OF "local", FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a recognised foreign degree`                          MEANS `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` OF "degree", TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a degree recognised against the Registrar's own opinion` MEANS `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` OF "degree", TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a foreign degree recognised on condition, condition met`     MEANS `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` OF "degree", TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a foreign degree recognised on condition, condition unmet`   MEANS `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` OF "degree", TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

-- Every precondition is needed: foreign institution, Council consulted, Council's advice validly given, the Registrar's opinion.
#ASSERT `s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` `a foreign degree whose scope and content do not match` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` `a qualification from an Israeli institution` TRUE TRUE

-- FORK F-19c-advice, alternative: consulted is enough.  The discriminating case: consulted, advice not validly given.
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 19(c)(1), alternative reading — a foreign qualification may be recognised once the Council was consulted` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c)(1), alternative reading — a foreign qualification may be recognised once the Council was consulted` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c)(1), alternative reading — a foreign qualification may be recognised once the Council was consulted` `a foreign degree whose scope and content do not match` TRUE

-- The power, traced.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(c)(1) — the Registrar may recognise the foreign qualification` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `recognise a certificate, degree or training from a foreign educational institution` `the Registrar` "degree" AT 8

-- EXPECT STANDING recognise a certificate, degree or training from a foreign educational institution
#TRACE `s 19(c)(1) — the Registrar may recognise the foreign qualification` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 90)

-- Without valid advice there is no power to recognise: nothing stands.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(c)(1) — the Registrar may recognise the foreign qualification` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 90)

§§ `Section 19(c)(2): what is considered, and the conditional recognition`

-- Fields: level | programme | scope | duration, each compared with the institutions the Training Division recognises.
`all four matters considered`     MEANS `Matters the Registrar considered under section 19(c)(2)` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`the level was not considered`    MEANS `Matters the Registrar considered under section 19(c)(2)` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`the programme was not considered` MEANS `Matters the Registrar considered under section 19(c)(2)` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`the scope was not considered`    MEANS `Matters the Registrar considered under section 19(c)(2)` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`the duration was not considered` MEANS `Matters the Registrar considered under section 19(c)(2)` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 19(c)(2) — the Registrar considered the level, programme, scope and duration of the studies` `all four matters considered`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c)(2) — the Registrar considered the level, programme, scope and duration of the studies` `the level was not considered`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c)(2) — the Registrar considered the level, programme, scope and duration of the studies` `the programme was not considered`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c)(2) — the Registrar considered the level, programme, scope and duration of the studies` `the scope was not considered`
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c)(2) — the Registrar considered the level, programme, scope and duration of the studies` `the duration was not considered`

-- The duty to consider, as four acts in parallel: all four discharge it; three leave the fourth standing.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(c)(2) — in a decision to recognise, the Registrar must consider the level, programme, scope and duration of the studies` "degree" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `consider the level of the foreign studies` `the Registrar` "degree" AT 1
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `consider the programme of the foreign studies` `the Registrar` "degree" AT 2
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `consider the scope of the foreign studies` `the Registrar` "degree" AT 3
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `consider the duration of the foreign studies` `the Registrar` "degree" AT 4

-- EXPECT STANDING consider the duration of the foreign studies
#TRACE `s 19(c)(2) — in a decision to recognise, the Registrar must consider the level, programme, scope and duration of the studies` "degree" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `consider the level of the foreign studies` `the Registrar` "degree" AT 1
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `consider the programme of the foreign studies` `the Registrar` "degree" AT 2
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `consider the scope of the foreign studies` `the Registrar` "degree" AT 3

-- The power to attach a condition: any of the three conditions may be chosen, and only where recognition is possible.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(c)(2) — the Registrar may make the recognition conditional on a test, training or both` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `make a recognition conditional` `the Registrar` "degree" `passing a professional test` AT 6

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(c)(2) — the Registrar may make the recognition conditional on a test, training or both` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `make a recognition conditional` `the Registrar` "degree" `both passing a professional test and completing training studies` AT 6

-- No power where recognition itself is not possible (the Council's advice was not validly given).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 19(c)(2) — the Registrar may make the recognition conditional on a test, training or both` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 90)

§§ `Section 19(c): the foreign qualification was recognised`

-- All limbs: recognised, may be recognised, four matters considered, and any condition met.
#ASSERT `s 19(c) — the foreign qualification was recognised under section 19(c)` `a recognised foreign degree` `all four matters considered` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(c) — the foreign qualification was recognised under section 19(c)` `a foreign degree recognised on condition, condition met` `all four matters considered` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c) — the foreign qualification was recognised under section 19(c)` `a foreign degree recognised on condition, condition unmet` `all four matters considered` TRUE TRUE
-- The Registrar did not recognise it.
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c) — the foreign qualification was recognised under section 19(c)` `a foreign degree whose scope and content match` `all four matters considered` TRUE TRUE
-- Recognised, but a matter was not considered.
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c) — the foreign qualification was recognised under section 19(c)` `a recognised foreign degree` `the scope was not considered` TRUE TRUE
-- Recognised, but the Council's advice was not validly given.
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c) — the foreign qualification was recognised under section 19(c)` `a recognised foreign degree` `all four matters considered` TRUE FALSE
-- Recognised, but the Council was not consulted at all.
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c) — the foreign qualification was recognised under section 19(c)` `a recognised foreign degree` `all four matters considered` FALSE FALSE
-- Recognised, but the Registrar was not of the opinion that scope and content match.
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c) — the foreign qualification was recognised under section 19(c)` `a degree recognised against the Registrar's own opinion` `all four matters considered` TRUE TRUE
